  "package": "os",
  "notes": "std::fs / std::env / std::process behind Go's API (Unix only). Errors are io::Error values carrying PathError, LinkError, SyscallError, the io/fs and os sentinels and Errno, printed with Go's messages; is_exist/is_not_exist/is_permission/is_timeout and Error::is(&err) classify them. Root (OpenRoot, OpenInRoot and every Root method), ProcAttr.Files and Process.WithHandle are rust_stdlib_sys::os, built on openat/unlinkat/... and fork/execve with Go's traversal rules; the root crate's own os::Root and os::start_process remain the std-only versions. Root results are differentially tested against Go in tools/os_check.py (root_probe) and the exec pieces in tools/exec_check.py. Getuid/Geteuid/Getgid/Getegid/Getppid/Getgroups/Hostname, Process.Pipe (a real pipe(2)/pipe2(O_CLOEXEC) pair of Files with deadlines), Signal, Chtimes, Link and the File deadline methods (pipes, terminals and sockets; ErrNoDeadline otherwise) are rust_stdlib_sys::os, the system-interface crate of ADR 0004, which calls the C library directly and is differentially tested against Go in tools/sys_check.py.",
